<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Aid workers freed from Ethiopia - EU.</title>
<headline>Aid workers freed from Ethiopia - EU.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Irish government said on Wednesday that a team of foreign aid workers which strayed from Somalia into Ethiopia had been freed from Ethiopian detention.</p>
<p>Minister of State for overseas aid Joan Burton said in a statement that the team was now in Belet Uen, Somalia, and would be travelling to the Kenyan capital, Nairobi, later on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Those detained were Save the Children Fund (SCF) staff and included an Irish woman, Anne Mulcahy, the field director of the British-based charity.</p>
<p>Burton said the release followed intensive talks between the Irish and Ethiopian authorities at the highest level.</p>
</text>
